red_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueyed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueyed/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueyed/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueyed/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueyed/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueyed/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/535730089","html_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/11102#issuecomment-535730089","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/11102","id":535730089,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzNTczMDA4OQ==","user":{"login":"deathlyfrantic","id":7629614,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2Mjk2MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7629614?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic","html_url":"https://github.com/deathlyfrantic","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-09-27T00:09:57Z","updated_at":"2019-09-27T00:09:57Z","body":"> Could not reproduce it on master.\r\n\r\nI filed in haste and didn't spell out all the necessary steps, I think, so if you didn't look at the linked issue you may not have had enough lines in the buffer. (I will edit to clarify.) It seems to happen only if there are 4+ lines in the buffer, and it's always the second word of line 4 where the `+` appears. It goes from this:\r\n<img width=\"632\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2019-09-26 at 8 59 17 AM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7629614/65732615-a20e2e80-e098-11e9-91fc-fefc3d6fbc0a.png\">\r\nTo this:\r\n<img width=\"632\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2019-09-26 at 9 00 25 AM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7629614/65732631-bfdb9380-e098-11e9-92df-78bc5161a172.png\">\r\n> What clipboard tool do you use? (:checkhealth provider)\r\n```\r\n## clipboard (optional)\r\n  - OK: Clipboard tool found: pbcopy\r\n```\r\n(Side note - I had to fix the first letter of \"clipboard\" because it got changed to a `+` when I copied that information.)\r\n\r\n> I assume this happens only with the \"+ and \"* clipboard registers?\r\n\r\nActually I just tested and it doesn't happen with `*`, just with `+`. Strangely though, with the `0` and `:` registers (and presumably others), the `s` in the the word \"something\" that I have selected in the first screenshot gets replaced with the register name. No highlighting though. This is super weird!\r\n<img width=\"632\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2019-09-26 at 8 08 24 PM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7629614/65732783-6aec4d00-e099-11e9-8ed2-3527aa8d1686.png\">\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/535730089/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"deathlyfrantic","id":7629614,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2Mjk2MTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7629614?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deathlyfrantic","html_url":"https://github.com/deathlyfrantic","followers_